e impairment of perirhinal cortical plasticity and recognition memory. Eur J Neurosci 2004;20(8):2214&#x02013;24. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15450101</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Westra</surname><given-names>HA</given-names></name><name><surname>Stewart</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name><name><surname>Teehan</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Johl</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Dozois</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Hill</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Benzodiazepine use associated with decreased memory for psychoeducation material in cognitive behavioral therapy for panic disorder</article-title><source>Cogn Ther Res</source><year>2004</year><volume>28</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>193</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1023/B:COTR.0000021540.15135.45</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Westra HA, Stewart SH, Teehan M, Johl K, Dozois DJ, Hill T. Benzodiazepine use associated with decreased memory for psychoeducation material in cognitive behavioral therapy for panic disorder. Cogn Ther Res 2004;28(2):193. </citation></ref><ref id="CR16"><label>16.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kan</surname><given-names>CC</given-names></name><name><surname>Breteler</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name><name><surname>Zitman</surname><given-names>FG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>High prevalence of benzodiazepine dependence in out-patient users, based on the DSM-III-R and ICD-10 criteria</article-title><source>Acta Psychiatr Scand</source><year>1997</year><volume>96</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>85</fpage><lpage>93</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1600-0447.1997.tb09911.x</pub-id></citation><citation c